%I A039718 #16 Sep 06 2026 00:39:21
%S A039718 1,2,9,113,6212,3702013,75268594037,116821009344139086,
%T A039718 26037572288890231087273755,1593393947888911904758963141670027545
%N A039718 Two-dimensional simplicial complexes on n labeled nodes.
%C A039718 Let A_{<=3}(n) be the number of antichains of nonempty subsets of [n], all of whose members have size at most 3, including the empty antichain. Then A_{<=3}(n) = Sum_{m=0..n} binomial(n,m)*a(m). - _Vladeta Jovovic_, Sep 05 2026
%D A039718 F. Harary and E. M. Palmer, Graphical enumeration, Academic Press, NY, 1973.
%D A039718 Vladeta Jovovic, On the number of two-dimensional simplicial complexes (in Russian), Metody i sistemy tekhnicheskoy diagnostiki, Vypusk 16, Mezhvuzovskiy zbornik nauchnykh trudov, Izdatelstvo Saratovskogo universiteta, 1991, p. 77.
%H A039718 Vladeta Jovovic, <a href="/A039718/a039718.cpp.txt">C++ program for computing a(10)</a>
%F A039718 a(n+1) = Sum_{[G]} (n!/|Aut(G)|) * 2^t(G) * Sum_{S subseteq V(G)} 2^e(G[S]), where the outer sum is over isomorphism classes of simple graphs G on n vertices, t(G) is the number of triangles of G, and e(G[S]) is the number of edges of the subgraph induced by S. - _Vladeta Jovovic_, Sep 05 2026
%e A039718 a(3) = 9. Omitting the vertices {1}, {2}, {3}, which occur in every complex, the nine complexes are: {}, {{1,2}}, {{1,3}}, {{2,3}}, {{1,2},{1,3}}, {{1,2},{2,3}}, {{1,3},{2,3}}, {{1,2},{1,3},{2,3}}, {{1,2},{1,3},{2,3},{1,2,3}}.
%K A039718 nonn,hard,more,nice,changed
%O A039718 1,2
%A A039718 _Vladeta Jovovic_
%E A039718 a(7)-a(10) from _Vladeta Jovovic_, Sep 05 2026
